        "original_id": "e29eef20-9e77-5f4c-9185-9fe9026c0024",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Corylopsis, Impatiens, Corylopsis pauciflora\n- Taxonomy: genera, species, Hamamelidaceae\n- Places: eastern Asia, China, Japan, Korea, the Himalayas, Taiwan, Northern Hemisphere, tropics\n\nFacts:\n- Corylopsis is a genus of nearly 30 shrub species in the witch hazel family Hamamelidaceae.\n- Corylopsis is native to eastern Asia, with most species endemic to China and some also found in Japan, Korea, and the Himalayas.\n- Impatiens is a genus of about 850 to 1,000 species of flowering plants.\n- Impatiens is widely distributed throughout the Northern Hemisphere and the tropics.\n- Corylopsis pauciflora, also called buttercup witch hazel or winter hazel, is a flowering plant species in the genus Corylopsis and the family Hamamelidaceae.\n- Corylopsis pauciflora is native to Taiwan and Japan.",
